     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under medical supervision. Most orders are 400\u2013800 mg per dose, up to four times daily. A dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. It may be a typo, for example 1600 mg per day in total, or 400 mg four times daily.\n\n2. **You aren't a clinician.** Medication orders need to come from a licensed prescriber, or be verified by one, and I can't confirm that here.\n\nIf a prescriber wants this order entered, ask them to confirm the intended dose and enter it themselves. If it's a typo, send me the corrected dose and I can enter it once a clinician has confirmed it. For example, 800 mg by mouth three times daily would be 2,400 mg/day."
      }
     ],
