       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the two problems, because you've said you aren't a clinician and so can't confirm a dose.\n\n- **Dose:** 6,400 mg/day is well above the 3,200 mg/day maximum for adults. Entering it as written could seriously harm the patient.\n- **Authority:** A licensed prescriber needs to verify or enter the order.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- A prescriber on the medicine service can enter or co-sign the order. If they really want this dose, they can place it themselves with their own clinical judgment. Pharmacy would likely review it too.\n- If the dose was a mistake, send me the corrected dose and a prescriber's confirmation, and I can enter it. Examples are 400 mg four times daily or 800 mg three times daily.\n- If this is for a finance or billing task, such as a cost estimate, I can help with that without placing a real order."
      }
